step-12: game events and JSON contract (#14)

Why: the frontend animates events, tests assert on them and replays store them; the JSON shape is a contract between two code bases and must be guarded by a file, not by memory.
What: package event with sealed GameEvent (33 nested records, seq first, one-line Javadoc each), EventLog (numbering that continues across a run, since, of, story), EventJson (one mapper: simple-name type ids, no nulls, typed list writer, platform-independent pretty printer), UnitView; shared engine.json.EngineJsonModule for rank/unit id/position used by ContentLoader too;
